Wave 8 extends prior [[Machine learning]], [[Reasoning]], [[Knowledge representation]], [[Perception]], [[Distributed system]], [[Memory]], [[Computer network]], [[Language]], and [[Human-computer interaction]] into public AI/agent foundations.

== Dependency order ==

<pre>
Artificial intelligence
 ├→ Intelligent agent
 │    ├→ Planning (artificial intelligence)
 │    ├→ Multi-agent system
 │    └→ Autonomous agent (artificial intelligence)
 ├→ Machine learning
 └→ Large language model
      └→ AI agent
           ├→ Planning (artificial intelligence)
           ├→ Tool use (artificial intelligence)
           ├→ Agent memory (artificial intelligence)
           └→ Multi-agent system
</pre>

== Normalized definitions ==

=== Artificial intelligence ===
Artificial intelligence is the field concerned with computational systems that perform tasks involving perception, reasoning, learning, planning, language, decision-making, action, and related capabilities associated with intelligent behavior.

=== Intelligent agent ===
An intelligent agent is a computational entity modeled as perceiving an environment and selecting actions to pursue objectives.

=== AI agent ===
An AI agent is a contemporary AI-powered system designed to carry out goal-directed multi-step tasks by selecting and executing actions, often with environmental feedback and often using foundation models, tools, memory/state, or planning components.

=== Planning (artificial intelligence) ===
AI planning is the computational problem of selecting or synthesizing actions that can move a system from an initial situation toward a goal under an action/environment model.

=== Tool use (artificial intelligence) ===
AI tool use is the selection, invocation, and incorporation of external functions/resources such as APIs, calculators, search systems, databases, code execution, software interfaces, or devices.

=== Agent memory (artificial intelligence) ===
Agent memory is persistent or selectively retained computational state that enables an artificial agent to use prior observations, interactions, actions, or learned experience in future decision-making.

=== Multi-agent system ===
A multi-agent system is a computational system composed of multiple interacting agents whose behavior can be cooperative, competitive, mixed-motive, coordinated, decentralized, or partially independent.

=== Autonomous agent (artificial intelligence) ===
An autonomous AI agent is an artificial agent that can select and execute actions over time with limited immediate external control, using its own policy/deliberation and feedback within defined objectives and constraints.

=== Large language model ===
A large language model is a large-scale statistical/neural language model trained over very large corpora to model and generate token sequences and commonly adapted to a wide range of downstream language tasks.

